g back to the first user message — confirmed against the live TUI. Fabricated sessions had no `ai-title`, so every bridge showed up under the same string, naming the machinery instead of the conversation. Now titled from the first human turn.\n\n**`estimateTokens` is gone.** It was `chars/4` — a byte count wearing a token costume, misleading twice over since token counts don't transfer across tokenizers and a bridge targets a different model by definition. Replaced with characters + utf8 bytes, now reported on the fabrication path too, which is the default and previously reported nothing.\n\n## Also resolved\n\n- **Large histories**: clean to 300 turns / ~215 KB on both targets, with markers planted in the *first* and last turns both recalled — early history is not dropped when a long history arrives all at once.\n- **Timestamps**: ordering is not load-bearing, so the notice stays at fabrication time. Format tolerance is still unmeasured, so we normalize to millisecond UTC on write rather than trusting it.\n- **Codex picker cwd filter**: exact string match, not a prefix — a subdirectory session is filtered out too. `--all` lifts it.\n- **`base_instructions`**: reclassified from open question to deliberate omission. The source session's real system prompt isn't in the ledger, so any value here would invent a claim about what the original session was told.\n\n## New probes\n\n`probe-session-invariants.mjs`, `probe-large-history.mjs`, `probe-codex-function-call.mjs`, `probe-picker.mjs` (pty-driven). All clean up after themselves; `PROBE_KEEP=1` retains artifacts.\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\nHistories past ~300 turns (fitting them is the target CLI's job), `custom_tool_call` fabrication, and which key the Claude picker sorts on.\n\n77 tests pass. This branch also carries 5 previously-unpushed commits from local `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TZemvnoFQ87rYijmXw5dbQ\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2"